ts/The-Deligne-Drinfeld-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":50,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"f3fd0616a2ddaa13672a15baa7de1d31e6f754d873eb0375a331e51b82c8c2b9","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Deligne-Drinfeld-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:575faba9097bc541e4d565d0f3d3d1d4dcdc47895f513f2da87ad20acd1c94bf","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Deligne-Drinfeld-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L50"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are homogeneous elements\n\\(\\sigma_{2k+1}\\in W_{2k+1}\\), one for each \\(k\\ge1\\), for which\n\\[\n \\Lie_{\\Q}\\langle e_3,e_5,e_7,\\ldots\\rangle\n \\longrightarrow (W,\\{\\, ,\\,\\}),\\qquad\n e_{2k+1}\\longmapsto\\sigma_{2k+1},\n\\]\nis an isomorphism of graded Lie algebras.\nIn particular, \\(W\\) is closed under the bracket\n\\eqref{eq:ihara}.  The induced map on completions by weight is a\ncontinuous graded isomorphism."}
